{
  "ceiling_parameterisation": {
    "quantity": "repetition_factor_r = demand / supply, per lane",
    "weakest_for_us": "their hardest extrapolation case is Swahili and their weakest predictions are on quality-tiered mixtures - i.e. exactly the Indic lane.",
    "why_per_lane": "arXiv:2605.12715 measures degradation as a function of each lane's OWN repetition factor, not a global epoch count. Scarcer lanes tolerate higher r (5x-smaller target -> r about 30; 5x-larger -> r < 7).",
    "why_the_level_is_unchanged": "the same paper measures optimal r and optimal target weight both FALLING with model size (9.5% at 101M -> 1.9% at 539M) and states that extrapolation beyond about 900M is open. We plan ~30B. Re-shaping the ceiling is free; raising it is an extrapolation the evidence does not support, so the level stays at 4.0 (arXiv:2305.16264)."
  },
  "dedup_sensitivity": {
